bhyve: virtio: the virtio 1.0 register interface next to the legacy one

bhyve's virtio devices have only the legacy interface: registers in an
I/O BAR.  A guest that cannot use I/O BARs has no way to drive them;
Windows on arm64 loads the virtio driver and then fails to start the
device.

Add the virtio 1.0 ("modern") interface in a memory BAR, described by
the four vendor capabilities, so that every device that uses
vi_set_io_bar() becomes a transitional device: common configuration
with 64-bit features and the three queue addresses, notification, ISR
and the device's own configuration.  VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1 is offered there
and passed to the device model's vc_apply_features(); virtio-net uses
the 12-byte header when it is negotiated.  The legacy interface is
unchanged; virtio.modern=false leaves the new one out.

pci_emul_add_capability() is exported for the capabilities.

